introduce local curvature. At the lower end of the carbon range, this may produce
an artificial decrease in retention times with increasing carbon number, while
at the upper end, predicted times may decrease after a local maximum-both
behaviors do not follow the theoretically expected elution pattern. To correct
this, retention times for lipids below a local minimum are adjusted to follow a
monotonic increasing slope based on the difference between the minimum and the
preceding lipid, while for lipids above a local maximum, retention times are
capped at the value of the maximum. These adjustments ensure that predicted
